      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If $∠X$ and $∠Y$ are complementary angles and $m∠X={47}^{∘}$, then $m∠Y=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14186058/assets/8079f80c1adad20a0844885f06cb56feb8fc55d8172aa154d4d2c484c3b977cc.png)\n\nSince $∠X$ and $∠Y$ are complementary, the sum of their measures is equal to ${90}^{∘}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠X+m∠Y & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ {47}^{∘}+m∠Y & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠Y & ={43}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
